    {
      "id": 7,
      "name": "Coloc",
      "description": "Colocalisation is set to 0.1 (0.1-1) as default and may be changed.\n\nWith these settings you will find the following groups:\n- @spots: contains spots outside the cells\n- @in-cell-spots: includes all spots that are within the cell(coloc and non-coloc spots)\n- @ in-cell-spot non coloc: spots only detected in the one respective channel\n- 2 channel coloc spots (e.g. ch1@in-cell-spots coloc ch2) includes all spots in cell that have channel 1 and 2 and also includes spots that might have ch3\n- 3 channel coloc spots: in-cell-spots recognized in ch1, 2 and 3\n Approximation notes: $colocalization N-way matrix approximated as pairwise Colocalization steps (each non-Undefined entry paired with the first other non-Undefined entry) $colocalization N-way matrix approximated as pairwise Colocalization steps (each non-Undefined entry paired with the first other non-Undefined entry) $colocalization N-way matrix approximated as pairwise Colocalization steps (each non-Undefined entry paired with the first other non-Undefined entry) $colocalization N-way matrix approximated as pairwise Colocalization steps (each non-Undefined entry paired with the first other non-Undefined entry)",
